From: P Praneesh <praneesh.p@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: report complete per-link station dumps

Remove the link level statistics handling from nl80211_send_station() and
drop the unused link_stats parameter from its signature and callers. The
removed code iterated over each MLO link and attempted to send link
specific station data through NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINKS, but this logic was
never used because link_stats was always false.

Add a helper function nl80211_put_sta_info_common() to pack the station-
level (aggregated) STA information into a netlink message. This prepares
the code for future enhancements such as supporting fragmented link
statistics in nl80211_dump_station.

Currently, nl80211_dump_station() relies on the netlink callback's generic
args array (cb->args[2]) to track the station index during dumps. It also
processes the entire sinfo structure and transmits it to userspace
immediately in a single pass.

In MLO scenarios, stations may have multiple links, each with distinct
statistics. When userspace tools like iw or hostapd request station dumps,
attempting to pack all per-link stats into a single netlink message can
easily exceed the default 4KB buffer limit, especially when more than two
links are active. This results in -EMSGSIZE errors and incomplete data
delivery.

Currently, when userspace requests station information with link statistics
using NL80211_CMD_GET_STATION with the NL80211_ATTR_STA_DUMP_LINK_STATS
flag, the kernel uses the .doit callback (nl80211_get_station) which sends
a single netlink message. For MLO stations with multiple links, the link
statistics can be large and may exceed the maximum netlink message size,
causing the operation to fail with -EMSGSIZE.

